+## SummitEverything: Sol + Luna workflow overlay (append only; do not replace existing rules)
+
+The existing project AGENTS.md, IMPLEMENTER.md, TESTER.md, acceptance matrix and milestone gates remain authoritative. When there is a conflict, follow the stricter existing project requirement; notify the human rather than weakening a gate.
+
+At the start of a new coding run, inspect the real repository state and read:
+- README.md
+- AGENTS.md
+- docs/handoff/IMPLEMENTER.md
+- docs/handoff/TESTER.md
+- docs/handoff/PROMPT-STAGE-B-C-LUNA.md
+- docs/handoff/LATEST-IMPLEMENTATION.md
+- docs/implementation/PROGRESS.md
+- docs/quality/ACCEPTANCE.md
+- docs/quality/reports/README.md
+- docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-09-summit-everything-v1.md
+
+The README dated 2026-10-10 describes Stage A as Fake-only accepted, and identifies main at 117086eb2075726730cd7aa62ea0b61498e96f0c at that time. Confirm current HEAD, working-tree status and current documentation before relying on this historical baseline. Do not reset or overwrite changes based only on the README.
+
+For the first rollout, implement a narrowly bounded Stage B offline task, with fake/isolated materials and independent QA. Stage C real-account verification is a SEPARATE opt-in gate and must not be started implicitly.
+
+Forbidden without the human's explicit, specific authorization: authentic Feishu/OAuth connections and writes; real model/provider traffic or quality claims; fetching, storing or exposing real work material; OS Keychain operations on real credentials; irreversible operations; changing or running against SWB, SK or the real _vault. Also keep DMG, five-day continuous run and two-machine acceptance as separate unverified gates until truly tested.
+
+Run only tests that fit the slice, following the implementation and tester manuals. The README includes these baseline commands:
+- uv run pytest -q
+- uv run ruff check src tests
+- uv run ruff format --check src tests
+- uv run mypy src
+- uv lock --check
+- uv build
+- npm --prefix web test
+- npm --prefix web run typecheck
+- npm --prefix web run lint
+- npm --prefix web run build
+
+For relevant browser/UI verification, consider the isolated local dev workflow described in the README (`uv run python scripts/run_dev.py`, local WebUI at http://127.0.0.1:5173), and report whether a browser-based check was actually performed. Do not assert native DMG or real-service acceptance from local WebUI tests.
+
+Source code and tracked tests must not be edited by the QA agent. QA evidence may only be written where TESTER.md/repository policy allows. Sol checks tested commit SHA, unexpected git status changes, and the tester's evidence before deciding merge eligibility.
+
+Before important milestone merges to main, ask the human for approval; Stage B closure is such a milestone. Respect existing project Git/handoff conventions, and do not invent a parallel governance system.
+
